  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1.899999976158142,
      "text": "Begin with the flower overview.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 2.700000047683716,
      "end": 7.267179418832828,
      "text": "A labels the stigma at the top of the central carpel, and H points to the",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 7.267179418832828,
      "end": 7.579999923706055,
      "text": "style",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 7.579999923706055,
      "end": 8.0600004196167,
      "text": "below it.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 8.479999542236328,
      "end": 12.359999656677246,
      "text": "B identifies an anther, with C indicating its supporting filament.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 13.039999961853027,
      "end": 15.119999885559082,
      "text": "Anther and filament together form a stamen.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 15.800000190734863,
      "end": 18.5,
      "text": "D points to a petal and E to a sepal.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 19.200000762939453,
      "end": 23.639999389648438,
      "text": "The drawing shows selected organs in a schematic longitudinal view, not the",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 23.639999389648438,
      "end": 26.5,
      "text": "exact number or proportion found in a particular species.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 27.059999465942383,
      "end": 30.459999084472656,
      "text": "Trace leader lines to their endpoints before naming a structure.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 31.260000228881836,
      "end": 35.720001220703125,
      "text": "Do not confuse the filament at C with the central style at H merely because",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 35.720001220703125,
      "end": 36.400001525878906,
      "text": "both are slender.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 36.86400000000051,
      "end": 38.72400001430562,
      "text": "Now compare F and G.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 39.403999961853536,
      "end": 43.684000171661886,
      "text": "F points to the wall of the ovary, while G points to an ovule inside it.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 44.76400009536794,
      "end": 49.02399984741262,
      "text": "Following normal seed development, an ovule becomes a seed and the ovary",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 49.02399984741262,
      "end": 53.36400000000051,
      "text": "usually develops into a fruit, sometimes with contributions from other floral",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 53.36400000000051,
      "end": 53.784000076294454,
      "text": "tissues.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 55.784000076294454,
      "end": 57.56400076293996,
      "text": "They are not interchangeable labels.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 58.52399984741262,
      "end": 61.64400068664602,
      "text": "D and E identify a petal and a sepal respectively.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 62.284000076294454,
      "end": 67.5440003051763,
      "text": "The stigma receives pollen; fertilisation occurs later after the appropriate",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 67.5440003051763,
      "end": 68.80400053405813,
      "text": "events within the ovule.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 69.78399816894583,
      "end": 72.92400137329153,
      "text": "A pollen grain on the stigma is therefore not already a seed.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 73.90400091552786,
      "end": 78.02399984741263,
      "text": "Keep the organ, its internal structure and its developmental fate as separate",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 78.02399984741263,
      "end": 78.96399847412161,
      "text": "parts of the explanation.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 79.32000000000123,
      "end": 81.83999998092774,
      "text": "The placentation figure has three panels.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 82.72000009536866,
      "end": 87.35999996185426,
      "text": "A is a longitudinally opened ovary with ovules attached along one margin,",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 88.20000011444215,
      "end": 89.43999988556031,
      "text": "illustrating marginal placentation.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 90.2800000381482,
      "end": 94.85999996185426,
      "text": "B is a transverse section with partitions meeting at a central axis where",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 94.85999996185426,
      "end": 97.87999946594361,
      "text": "ovules attach: this is axile placentation.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 98.79999954223756,
      "end": 102.86000091552857,
      "text": "C is also a transverse section, but the ovules attach to the inner peripheral",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 102.86000091552857,
      "end": 105.13999969482545,
      "text": "wall in the illustrated parietal pattern.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 106.08000022888307,
      "end": 109.8400004577649,
      "text": "Read the section labels L S and T S before comparing the panels.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 110.66000015258912,
      "end": 114.06000167846803,
      "text": "Different views can reveal different features, so do not treat the elongated",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 114.06000167846803,
      "end": 117.45999938964967,
      "text": "outline in A as evidence that it belongs to a completely different organ.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 118.18000061035279,
      "end": 120.75999862671021,
      "text": "The shared question is where the ovules attach.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 120.98400000000191,
      "end": 123.18400004768563,
      "text": "Look again at B and C.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 123.92400005722237,
      "end": 128.20399979019356,
      "text": "B contains partitions, or septa, extending from the wall toward the central",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 128.20399979019356,
      "end": 128.54399994278145,
      "text": "axis.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 129.4239995803852,
      "end": 131.28400019073678,
      "text": "This supports the axile interpretation.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 132.22399977112008,
      "end": 135.88553806637685,
      "text": "A centrally positioned placenta without these partitions can instead",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 135.88553806637685,
      "end": 136.4239995803852,
      "text": "illustrate",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 136.4239995803852,
      "end": 140.1640003051777,
      "text": "a free central pattern, which is not drawn as a separate panel here.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 140.92400053405953,
      "end": 145.22399977112008,
      "text": "In C, ovules are peripheral rather than attached to the illustrated central",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 145.22399977112008,
      "end": 145.64399984741402,
      "text": "axis.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 146.44399908447457,
      "end": 151.18400076294137,
      "text": "Real ovaries may have additional features, including false partitions, so a",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 151.18400076294137,
      "end": 155.34400061035348,
      "text": "simple diagram is a teaching model rather than a universal species diagnosis.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 156.44399908447457,
      "end": 160.02400091552926,
      "text": "Name the attachment and supporting structures you can actually see before",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 160.02400091552926,
      "end": 161.40399816894723,
      "text": "applying a memorised example.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 162.3240001525898,
      "end": 165.30399969482613,
      "text": "Letter B does not always mean axile in another question.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 165.55200000000272,
      "end": 168.89199991417203,
      "text": "The plant tissue comparison shows schematic cell sections.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 169.59199996185575,
      "end": 173.65200038147245,
      "text": "A has relatively thin walls, represented nuclei and intercellular spaces,",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 174.3920001525906,
      "end": 175.3920001525906,
      "text": "fitting typical parenchyma.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 176.27200026703153,
      "end": 180.3319997329739,
      "text": "B shows living cells with uneven thickening at the corners, the familiar",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 180.3319997329739,
      "end": 181.21199984741483,
      "text": "collenchyma pattern.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 182.01199908447538,
      "end": 186.41200061035428,
      "text": "C shows thick walls around narrow lumens, with no living protoplast",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 186.41200061035428,
      "end": 188.33200068664823,
      "text": "represented, fitting mature sclerenchyma.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 188.8920001525906,
      "end": 191.91200061035428,
      "text": "The clear central spaces in C are not nuclei.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 192.59200091553006,
      "end": 196.1119994659451,
      "text": "Wall chemistry and developmental context are additional evidence in a real",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 196.1119994659451,
      "end": 199.79200167846952,
      "text": "specimen; a cartoon does not perform a chemical test for lignin.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 200.71199984741483,
      "end": 204.7320003051785,
      "text": "Use the combination of living state, wall distribution and lumen rather than",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 204.7320003051785,
      "end": 206.61200137329374,
      "text": "calling every thick walled cell sclerenchyma.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 207.36000000000342,
      "end": 210.36000000000342,
      "text": "Keep the same tissue panels and add function carefully.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 211.06000004768714,
      "end": 215.0999997711216,
      "text": "Parenchyma at A can support storage or metabolism, and some parenchyma cells",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 215.0999997711216,
      "end": 217.36000000000342,
      "text": "photosynthesise.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 217.36000000000342,
      "end": 221.3200000381504,
      "text": "A thin walled cell in a schematic does not by itself prove that it contains",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 221.3200000381504,
      "end": 222.21999965668067,
      "text": "chloroplasts.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 222.21999965668067,
      "end": 226.7599996185337,
      "text": "Collenchyma at B supplies flexible support in familiar growing organs.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 228.12000022888526,
      "end": 232.08820514288047,
      "text": "Mature sclerenchyma at C typically provides strong support through thick,",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 232.08820514288047,
      "end": 232.36000000000342,
      "text": "often",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 232.36000000000342,
      "end": 235.28000007629737,
      "text": "lignified walls after loss of the living protoplast.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 235.96000038147315,
      "end": 239.9400018310581,
      "text": "These are standard functional comparisons, not claims that each tissue has",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 239.9400018310581,
      "end": 241.42000137329444,
      "text": "exactly one role everywhere.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 242.76000152588233,
      "end": 245.83512802711243,
      "text": "State which observed structural clue supports the function and what",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 245.83512802711243,
      "end": 246.33999954223975,
      "text": "information",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 246.33999954223975,
      "end": 247.58000122070655,
      "text": "the drawing does not provide.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 247.87200000000408,
      "end": 251.13199999046734,
      "text": "The animal tissue figure uses three simplified views.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 251.95199992371013,
      "end": 255.4119999618571,
      "text": "A shows a single layer of flattened epithelial cells on a basement membrane,",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 255.79200007629802,
      "end": 257.87200000000405,
      "text": "fitting simple squamous epithelium.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 258.55200030517983,
      "end": 262.8935383676423,
      "text": "B shows cells distributed among fibres in an extracellular matrix, a",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 262.8935383676423,
      "end": 263.53199984741616,
      "text": "connective",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 263.53199984741616,
      "end": 264.1119997711222,
      "text": "tissue pattern.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 265.05200030517983,
      "end": 269.44584667030153,
      "text": "C shows parallel striated skeletal muscle fibres with several peripheral",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 269.44584667030153,
      "end": 269.81200053406167,
      "text": "nuclei",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 269.81200053406167,
      "end": 270.37200000000405,
      "text": "represented.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 271.3519995422404,
      "end": 274.8519995422404,
      "text": "Do not treat the different panel heights as measured tissue thicknesses,",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 274.8519995422404,
      "end": 278.4519999237101,
      "text": "because the drawings use different viewing orientations and arbitrary scales.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 279.31200053406167,
      "end": 283.77200152588296,
      "text": "A tissue identification should use arrangement, matrix, cell form and other",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 283.77200152588296,
      "end": 284.77200152588296,
      "text": "relevant clues together.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 285.3319990844767,
      "end": 288.8613340454145,
      "text": "A round mark in one image can be a nucleus or a sectioned structure; its",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 288.8613340454145,
      "end": 289.08000000000476,
      "text": "context matters.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 289.08000000000476,
      "end": 290.54000003815173,
      "text": "Finish with C.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 291.6599999237108,
      "end": 295.9861537155786,
      "text": "Striations support a striated muscle identification, but cardiac muscle is",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 295.9861537155786,
      "end": 296.21999986649035,
      "text": "also",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 296.21999986649035,
      "end": 296.6199999618578,
      "text": "striated.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 297.60000045776843,
      "end": 301.54666697967224,
      "text": "The parallel, unbranched fibres and multiple peripheral nuclei represented",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 301.54666697967224,
      "end": 301.76000030518054,
      "text": "here",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 301.76000030518054,
      "end": 303.8800001907396,
      "text": "support the skeletal muscle interpretation.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 304.8199997711229,
      "end": 309.45999916077136,
      "text": "A small section or poor image can hide branching, nuclei or junctions, so a",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 309.45999916077136,
      "end": 311.7800007629442,
      "text": "single stripe is not a complete diagnostic key.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 312.70000083923816,
      "end": 316.8799992370653,
      "text": "A at the top is an epithelial lining rather than a muscle layer, and B",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 316.8799992370653,
      "end": 322.10000045776843,
      "text": "emphasises extracellular matrix rather than parallel contractile fibres.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 322.10000045776843,
      "end": 326.07752957633846,
      "text": "Explain why your chosen answer fits several features, then state a limit of",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 326.07752957633846,
      "end": 326.82000167847156,
      "text": "the schematic.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 328.1200009155321,
      "end": 332.5228205245628,
      "text": "These figures teach structural recognition and do not identify a disease from",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 332.5228205245628,
      "end": 332.58000000000476,
      "text": "a",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 332.58000000000476,
      "end": 332.9400006103563,
      "text": "tissue image.",
      "chapter": 7
    }
  ]
}
